    "question": "Jules is walking dogs to help pay for his family's vacation. The vacation costs $1,000. There are five members in his family and each one must contribute the same amount towards the vacation cost. He charges $2 to start a walk and $1.25 per block. If he walks 20 dogs, how many blocks in total does he have to walk them?",
    "gold": "128",
    "answer": "Jules has to earn $200 because 1000 / 5 = <<1000/5=200>>200\nHe has earned $40 from starting the walks because 20 x 2 = <<20*2=40>>40\nHe has to earn $160 from distance, because 200 - 40 = <<200-40=160>>160\nHe has to walk 128 blocks because 160 / 1.25 = <<160/1.25=128>>128\n#### 128"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many blocks Jules has to walk the dogs, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total contribution each family member must make:**\n   The total cost of the vacation is $1,000, and there are five family members. Therefore, each family member must contribute:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1000}{5} = 200 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the total amount Jules earns from walking the dogs:**\n   Jules charges $2 to start a walk and $1.25 per block. If he walks 20 dogs, the total number of blocks he walks is:\n   \\[\n   20 \\text{ dogs} \\times 20 \\text{ blocks per dog} = 400 \\text{ blocks}\n   \\]\n   The total amount Jules earns from walking the dogs is:\n   \\[\n   400 \\text{ blocks} \\times 1.25 \\text{ dollars per block} = 500 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Verify the total contribution:**\n   Jules earns $500 from walking the dogs. Since each family member must contribute $200, the total contribution from all family members is:\n   \\[\n   5 \\text{ family members} \\times 200 \\text{ dollars per family member} = 1000 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n   This matches the total cost of the vacation, confirming our calculations are correct.\n\n4. **Calculate the total number of blocks walked:**\n   As calculated earlier, Jules walks 400 blocks in total.\n\nTherefore, the total number of blocks Jules has to walk the dogs is \\(\\boxed{400}\\).",
